.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt KQUEUE 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm kern_kqueue ,
.Nm kern_kevent
.Nd kernel event queues for the BSD personalities
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/kqueue.h
.Ft int
.Fn kern_kqueue "void"
.Ft int
.Fo kern_kevent
.Fa "int kq"
.Fa "const struct kq_event *changes"
.Fa "int nchanges"
.Fa "struct kq_event *events"
.Fa "int nevents"
.Fa "int timeout_ms"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These implement
.Xr kqueue 2
and
.Xr kevent 2
as the BSDs have them.
Substrate's own programs do not call them; a personality whose programs
do converts its layout of
.Vt struct kevent
to and from
.Vt struct kq_event
and calls these.
The FreeBSD personality does, for system calls 362, 363, 560 and 583.
.Pp
.Fn kern_kqueue
makes an empty queue and returns a descriptor for it in the calling
process.
.Pp
.Fn kern_kevent
applies
.Fa nchanges
changes to the queue, then collects up to
.Fa nevents
events into
.Fa events ,
waiting
.Fa timeout_ms
milliseconds for the first:
\-1 waits until there is one, 0 does not wait.
Both arrays are the kernel's.
.Pp
A registration is named by its
.Va ident
and
.Va filter .
The filters are:
.Bl -tag -width "KQ_EVFILT_WRITE"
.It Dv KQ_EVFILT_READ
.Va ident
is a descriptor; reported when
.Xr poll 2
would report it readable, hung up or in error.
.It Dv KQ_EVFILT_WRITE
The same for writing.
.It Dv KQ_EVFILT_USER
.Va ident
is the program's own.
Reported after a change carrying
.Dv KQ_NOTE_TRIGGER ;
the low 24 bits of
.Va fflags
are combined as
.Dv KQ_NOTE_FFAND ,
.Dv KQ_NOTE_FFOR
or
.Dv KQ_NOTE_FFCOPY
say.
.It Dv KQ_EVFILT_TIMER
.Va ident
is the program's own.
Reported every
.Va data
milliseconds, or seconds, microseconds or nanoseconds with the
.Dv KQ_NOTE_*
unit flags;
.Va data
of the event is the number of periods since the last report.
.El
.Pp
.Dv KQ_EV_ADD
makes a registration,
.Dv KQ_EV_DELETE
removes one,
.Dv KQ_EV_ENABLE
and
.Dv KQ_EV_DISABLE
turn its reporting on and off.
.Dv KQ_EV_ONESHOT ,
.Dv KQ_EV_DISPATCH
and
.Dv KQ_EV_CLEAR
say what becomes of it once reported (removed, disabled, reset) and are
fixed when it is made: adding it again does not change them.
Every change replaces the registration's
.Va udata
unless it carries
.Dv KQ_EV_KEEPUDATA .
.Pp
A change that fails, or that carries
.Dv KQ_EV_RECEIPT ,
is answered with an event whose
.Va flags
are
.Dv KQ_EV_ERROR
and whose
.Va data
is the error number, 0 for a receipt.
If any such events were produced the call returns them without waiting.
A failure when
.Fa events
has no room for it ends the call with that error.
.Pp
A registration for a descriptor goes when the descriptor is closed.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn kern_kqueue
returns the new descriptor.
.Fn kern_kevent
returns the number of events placed in
.Fa events ,
which is 0 when the time ran out.
Both return a negated error number on failure.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
.Fa kq
is not a queue, has been closed, or belongs to another process; or a
change names a descriptor that is not open.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
A count is negative, the filter is not one of the four, or a timer's
period is negative or absolute.
.It Bq Er ENOENT
A change other than an add names a registration that does not exist.
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
No memory, or the queue already holds 4096 registrations.
.It Bq Er EMFILE
The process has no descriptor free.
.It Bq Er EINTR
A signal arrived during the wait.
.El
.Sh IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
Readiness of descriptors is taken from the per-file poll hooks through
.Fn kern_poll .
A thread with nothing to collect waits there on the registered
descriptors and on the queue's own, which is readable when a user event
has fired; that is how a trigger from another thread wakes it.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr poll 2
.Sh BUGS
.Dv KQ_EV_CLEAR
on a descriptor reports once each time it goes from not ready to ready,
not each time more arrives while it is ready.
.Pp
.Va data
of a read or write event is 1 when the descriptor is ready and 0 when it
has only hung up, not a byte count.
.Pp
A forked child inherits the descriptor and gets
.Er EBADF
from it; on a BSD the child does not have it at all.
.Pp
.Dv EVFILT_VNODE ,
.Dv EVFILT_PROC
and
.Dv EVFILT_SIGNAL
are not implemented.
